entries unchanged.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 & -7 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -5 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 0 & 5 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The minimum set is $a_{31}$. Replace this entry with $0$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 & -7 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -5 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 0 & 5 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\longrightarrow\\,\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 & -7 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe nonzero rows have leading entries in columns 1, 2, 3, in strictly increasing order, and all zero rows are at the bottom. \n\nRestoring $a_{31}$ would put the leading entry of row 3 in column 1, which is not to the right of the leading entry in row 2. The original matrix is not in row echelon form, so at least one replacement is needed.\n\nEntries to the right of a leading entry may remain nonzero."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186619071 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129115 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe0050b2-b5bc-54a6-aeaf-94cd5d7e5dfb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Operations That Would Transform a Matrix To Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1463fadc-18b9-5abe-aeff-7a02c62cc005" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a_{12}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186650396} {:answer/id #uuid "18e269ff-b8ad-50ce-905b-002c78d9eb0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a_{11}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186650397} {:answer/id #uuid "b2cd9fbe-e128-590f-8219-440402b105f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a_{14}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186650410} {:answer/id #uuid "c9b6a38f-20a9-5063-8e9e-23e2beccace0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a_{22}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186650415} {:answer/id #uuid "d74c92f6-4d15-5b75-95af-041e19fc8fcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a_{21}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186650417}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d74c92f6-4d15-5b75-95af-041e19fc8fcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a_{21}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186650417} :answer-field/id #uuid "d91ac81a-c547-54e5-aa3a-08388c0c02e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619096}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0f10b9b7-6897-5439-aaf8-a54e014b3de3" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A$ below. Which set of entries should be replaced by $0$ to obtain row echelon form **using the fewest replacements**? Leave all other entries unchanged.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -6 & -9 & -5 \\\\ -5 & -3 & 5 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The minimum set is $a_{21}$. Replace this entry with $0$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -6 & -9 & -5 \\\\ -5 & -3 & 5 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\longrightarrow\\,\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -6 & -9 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 5 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe nonzero rows have leading entries in columns 1, 2, 3, 4, in strictly increasing order, and all zero rows are at the bottom. \n\nRestoring $a_{21}$ would put the leading entry of row 2 in column 1, which is not to the right of the leading entry in row 1. The original matrix is not in row echelon form, so at least one replacement is needed.\n\nEntries to the right of a leading entry may remain nonzero."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186619077 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129115 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe0050b2-b5bc-54a6-aeaf-94cd5d7e5dfb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Operations That Would Transform a Matrix To Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ba2d607-0849-5274-b953-3b9e44a262eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a_{21}$, $a_{34}$, and $a_{43}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186650401} {:answer/id #uuid "875bd152-5f63-570c-a243-402abd704c6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a_{21}$, $a_{32}$, and $a_{43}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186650403} {:answer/id #uuid "b8a94230-e3d3-5208-9e3d-3cefed4b36fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a_{23}$, $a_{24}$, and $a_{44}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186650411} {:answer/id #uuid "bd239d43-da7b-5585-bb57-5ffd357ed357" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a_{13}$, $a_{43}$, and $a_{44}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186650412} {:answer/id #uuid "c0bdce41-9d53-5531-90d8-420301ad639a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a_{12}$, $a_{13}$, and $a_{34}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186650413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "875bd152-5f63-570c-a243-402abd704c6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a_{21}$, $a_{32}$, and $a_{43}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186650403} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f3f064b-6cc0-531f-8ae0-6e7a22948642" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619085}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "52005e0b-5fbd-516a-9d35-53afe7383c9e" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A$ below. Which set of entries should be replaced by $0$ to obtain row echelon form **using the fewest replacements**? Leave all other entries unchanged.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 & 7 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 8 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -7 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The minimum set is $a_{21}$, $a_{32}$, and $a_{43}$. Replace these 3 entries with $0$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 & 7 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 8 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -7 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\longrightarrow\\,\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe nonzero rows have leading entries in columns 1, 2, 3, 4, in strictly increasing order, and all zero rows are at the bottom. \n\nRestoring $a_{21}$ would put the leading entry of row 2 in column 1, which is not to the right of the leading entry in row 1. Restoring $a_{32}$ would put the leading entry of row 3 in column 2, which is not to the right of the leading entry in row 2. Restoring $a_{43}$ would put the leading entry of row 4 in column 3, which is not to the right of the leading entry in row 3. No set with fewer than 3 replacements satisfies both the leading-entry order and zero-row conditions.\n\nEntries to the right of a leading entry may remain nonzero."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186619080 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129115 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe0050b2-b5bc-54a6-aeaf-94cd5d7e5dfb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Operations That Would Transform a Matrix To Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24f43bab-78e2-5a3b-a4d8-e7ed10b62e4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a_{34}$ and $a_{43}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186650400} {:answer/id #uuid "7b3aaf3e-4da7-54a1-b681-ccc9db6ee094" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a_{11}$ and $a_{43}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186650402} {:answer/id #uuid "9a8cf554-be9d-59f5-ab80-988f392184ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a_{11}$ and $a_{24}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186650406} {:answer/id #uuid "9d899e95-e9e8-57cb-a8b7-14f27b160d6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a_{42}$ and $a_{43}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186650407 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186649259}]} {:answer/id #uuid "afc748c2-36f2-57b7-8d42-19e4bff203a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a_{11}$ and $a_{23}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186650409}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d899e95-e9e8-57cb-a8b7-14f27b160d6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a_{42}$ and $a_{43}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186650407} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3a12e32-4b12-57b9-990a-a712d3ea68ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619093}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "63d3f39d-4a1c-5646-9607-234dd8196589" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A$ below. Which set of entries should be replaced by $0$ to obtain row echelon form **using the fewest replacements**? Leave all other entries unchanged.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The minimum set is $a_{42}$ and $a_{43}$. Replace these 2 entries with $0$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\longrightarrow\\,\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe nonzero rows have leading entries in columns 1, 3, 4, in strictly increasing order, and all zero rows are at the bottom. \n\nRestoring $a_{42}$ would put the leading entry of row 4 in column 2, which is not to the right of the leading entry in row 3. Restoring $a_{43}$ would put the leading entry of row 4 in column 3, which is not to the right of the leading entry in row 3. No set with fewer than 2 replacements satisfies both the leading-entry order and zero-row conditions.\n\nEntries to the right of a leading entry may remain nonzero."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186619098 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129115 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe0050b2-b5bc-54a6-aeaf-94cd5d7e5dfb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Operations That Would Transform a Matrix To Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "105a5f49-10ed-59f1-adf5-8a93d04e7b06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a_{12}$ and $a_{41}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186650395} {:answer/id #uuid "21ae93fc-2646-5c1f-bc40-a6da936471ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a_{13}$ and $a_{34}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186650398} {:answer/id #uuid "a54ddd4d-e280-51df-858a-35638fa00a1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a_{41}$ and $a_{42}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186650408} {:answer/id #uuid "cf81a229-2285-5be9-81d8-32dfc381100d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a_{34}$ and $a_{41}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186650416} {:answer/id #uuid "d8000620-9752-506e-85d3-63ca996175ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a_{14}$ and $a_{42}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186650418}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a54ddd4d-e280-51df-858a-35638fa00a1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a_{41}$ and $a_{42}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186650408} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b4d2955-470a-51fe-a8df-ca668d6788a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619081}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "df625ae9-9615-5f6b-9178-1d3eaf0fa94f" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A$ below. Which set of entries should be replaced by $0$ to obtain row echelon form **using the fewest replacements**? Leave all other entries unchanged.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 6 & -9 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The minimum set is $a_{41}$ and $a_{42}$. Replace these 2 entries with $0$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 6 & -9 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\longrightarrow\\,\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 6 & -9 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe nonzero rows have leading entries in columns 1, 2, 4, in strictly increasing order, and all zero rows are at the bottom. \n\nRestoring $a_{41}$ would put the leading entry of row 4 in column 1, which is not to the right of the leading entry in row 3. Restoring $a_{42}$ would put the leading entry of row 4 in column 2, which is not to the right of the leading entry in row 3. No set with fewer than 2 replacements satisfies both the leading-entry order and zero-row conditions.\n\nEntries to the right of a leading entry may remain nonzero."}]}
